# OpenSigner: mount the kernel filesystems, run the shell, power the board
# off when it exits. There is no getty and no console login; the panel and
# the touch controller are the whole user interface.
#
# The shell's arguments describe the panel and are generated from the
# panel directory's panel.conf; /etc/opensigner/args is one line of them.
#
# The app is not root (security review 2026-09-11, M8): `setpriv --nnp`
# gives up the right to gain privileges through an exec, and `setuidgid`
# drops to the `opensigner` user, which owns the panel, the touch
# controller, the capture device and the files on the card, and nothing
# else. The card's raw block devices, /dev/i2c-* and the boot partition
# are root's, and root is only init.
::sysinit:/etc/init.d/rcS
::wait:/bin/sh -c 'exec /bin/setpriv --nnp /usr/bin/setuidgid opensigner /usr/bin/opensigner-pi $(cat /etc/opensigner/args)'
# Powering the board off is init's, not the app's: the app exits, and this
# is the next line init runs.
::wait:/sbin/poweroff -f
